        <zone forceUpdate='true' h='3667' id='16' type-v2='text' w='15643' x='39143' y='27800'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#f28e2b' fontsize='14'>Items Cap Enabled</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone forceUpdate='true' h='14600' id='17' type-v2='text' w='96000' x='1429' y='86000'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#ff8244' fontname='Tableau Bold' fontsize='12'>CAVEAT</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run>1. The snapshots in the datasource regarding capturing the quantity capping are from </run>
            <run bold='true'>June&apos;24</run>
            <run>, hence no prior data is available</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run>2. After alignment with the business stakeholders, the cap enabled and changed is as of the month where the item cap was changed, example: </run>
            <run bold='true'>if the item cap was changed on 1st August then only its captured, if the cap was changed on 30th July then it won&apos;t be considered in the reporting for August</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run>3. The item cap snapshots is of the </run>
            <run bold='true'>available</run>
            <run> items only, if the item was unavailable at the time of cap change, but became available later then the latter event will be captured, however if the cap has been changed but the item is unavailable since, then it wont be captured</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run>4. If an item cap has been changed more than once a day, then the</run>
            <run bold='true'> latest</run>
            <run> snapshot of cap is captured only</run>
          </formatted-text>
          <zone-style>
            <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
            <format attr='border-style' value='solid' />
            <format attr='border-width' value='1' />
          </zone-style>
        </zone>
